[MUSEai]@{role:{doe-expert}}

Owner adjustment (2026-11-01, direct in live-builds lane) adopted family-wide as DOE-FAMILY binding rule 7: n=3 floor, dynamically adjusted — sets of 3 per trigger, fresh instances per set, instance_key + set index + cumulative n stamped; stop on conclusive, +1 set on 2-1/noise; cap n=12/trigger (4 pre-registered looks) or campaign bound; cap = inconclusive datum.

INCIDENT (self-caught, disclosed): this PR also RESTORES rule 6. Verification for rule 7's anchor revealed rule 6 missing from master: PR #3145 (my own design+implement PR) was published from a scratch checkout taken before PR #3140 merged, and its DOE-FAMILY.md silently reverted rule 6 while adding the util-1 row (the ancient-base clobber pattern). Rule 6 text restored verbatim from d0ef64ad46. Process fix on my side: every payload file gets diffed against current master before publish, no exceptions.

[MUSEai]@{role:{doe-expert}}

First-contact fix, found by running the auditor against live master data before its first scheduled run: desk-feed/v1.3 carries dispatch stamps at traversals[].provider_usage[] (not a top-level dispatches list), and quota.registry.v2 carries the bench at services[] (not providers[]). Auditor now reads both actual shapes (with forward-compat fallbacks).

Proof run against master: scored = 3 (the live D1 stamps: DeepSeek 11:18:21Z, Gemini 11:19:22Z, Jules 11:44:17Z — outcomes null, in flight), flagged = 7 (historical provider_usage rows without ts — observational, as designed). First audit records included.

[MUSEai]@{role:{doe-expert}}

Owner order 2026-10-31: "This design implementation is required to automate the experiments for your review && adjustments."

Binding rule 5 added to DOE-FAMILY: every admitted campaign names its automation in DESIGN `automation{}` (runner/workflow that executes, emits records, produces SUMMARY); the loop is automation runs -> records land -> doe-expert reviews -> adjustments land as amendments. Unbuilt automation = admitted_design_only; manual runs = OBSERVATIONAL. Implementation work orders issued to the manager tree (live-3 dispatcher, live-1 ledger auditor, cb-1 acceptance CI; live-2 replay already follows the pattern).
